Same change as mihon-harmony 0012. On HarmonyOS 卓易通 the system side of
the process writes hundreds of graphics-layer errors per minute into the
app's logcat (BLASTBufferQueue "Faking releaseBufferCallback",
SurfaceDelegator "client is nullptr", HwViewRootImpl, HwAssetManagerEx,
"Display : result is null"). They fill the logcat buffer within minutes,
so a crash log dump rarely contains anything the app itself logged.

- CrashLogUtil reads logcat through a pipe instead of letting logcat write
  the file, drops lines matching the known noise markers and writes how
  many of each were dropped in the section header.
- HarmonyLogBuffer (byte-identical to the Mihon file) is a LogcatLogger
  that keeps the last 600 lines logged through logcat {} by the app
  (DEBUG and above, with timestamps); App.kt registers it next to
  AndroidLogcatLogger / XLogLogcatLogger and the dump appends its
  contents as an "App log" section.
